  Pre-Android 12 backup rules (android:fullBackupContent).

  OpenTV stores provider credentials (Xtream username/password, Stalker MAC, SMB password)
  in plaintext, on-device, by design: there is no OpenTV account and no server to hold them.
  That makes the device's own storage the only correct place for them — and makes Android
  Auto Backup, which would upload the app's private directory to the user's Google Drive,
  the one path by which they could leave it.

  Everything is excluded. A restored copy would carry a provider's line to a different
  device, out of the user's sight. Nothing here is worth that.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
